@kind(writ)

=[ Writ: workspace root ]

Rules the sisho-desk repository obeys.

Only the author edits this file. An agent that finds a rule in its way
proposes an edit here and stops. It does not work around the rule, and it
does not relax the rule to fit the change it wanted to make.

==[ crate-layering ]

@rule(crate-layering){
  guard: { twrit: layers }

  layers: {
    2: list( "app" )
    1: list( "crates/sisho-desk-tui" )
    0: list( "crates/sisho-desk-core" )
  }
}

Every workspace member belongs to exactly one layer, and depends only on
layers strictly below its own. Same-layer dependencies are allowed;
upward ones are not.

Layer 0 holds the desk core (the engine and state machine). Layer 1 holds
the TUI presentation and terminal driver. Layer 2 is the CLI program.

==[ no-sisho-crates ]

@rule(no-sisho-crates){
  guard: { twrit: door }

  door: {
    names: list( "sisho_run", "sisho_tools", "sisho_vault", "sisho_serve", "sisho_tui", "sisho_cli" )
    allowed: list()
  }
}

`sisho-desk` depends on no `sisho-*` crate. The extension knows the contract,
not the orchestrator.

==[ tmtroot-output-not-edited ]

@rule(tmtroot-output-not-edited){
  guard: { runs: "just docs-check" }
}

A file exported from @dir(tmtroot/) is generated. Do not hand-edit it. Edit
the source and re-export.
